    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "net, http: always set accepted sockets as non-blocking",
    "user": {
      "login": "darosior",
      "id": 22457751,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDU3NzUx",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22457751?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/darosior",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/darosior/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "A mistake here would be critical, as it would allow a malicious peer to stall us indefinitely for free. This is not currently an issue because:\n- while on Linux accepted sockets do not inherit O_NONBLOCK, we always send() and recv() on Linux/macOS/BSD with MSG_DONTWAIT;\n- while on Windows MSG_DONTWAIT is unset, accepted sockets do inherit the non-blocking option [^1].\n\nTherefore, set accepted sockets (inbound P2P connections and HTTP clients) as non-blocking explicitly, like CreateSockOS() does for the sockets it creates. A belt-and-suspenders check costs virtually nothing here, and we already have similar ones for less important options (such as TCP_NODELAY, which as far as i know is inherited by accepted sockets on all our supported platforms).\n\n[^1]: Source is [this](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winsock2/nf-winsock2-accept#remarks) implicit remark in the accept() doc, plus my own testing.",
